{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>You make me know</b> — for at the death of the body, then You will make me know the path of life. And the meaning: the path by which I will ascend to the heavens, to be with the angels of the Most High." "And the meaning of <b>satisfactions of joys before Your face</b> — that he will enjoy the splendor of the Shekhinah." "And the meaning of <b>You make me know</b> — for then the soul will be strengthened from the affairs of the world and will see eye to eye the truth." "And the meaning of <b>pleasantness in Your right hand</b> — that one will take pleasure in HaShem." "And the meaning of <b>in Your right hand</b> — like one who gives gifts of pleasantness to his beloved in his right hand." "And the meaning of <b>forever</b> — that His gifts will never cease, and behold, the reward of the righteous is explicitly stated in this psalm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:23.689645905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}